      "title": "Slate and Operations Specialist (Onsite)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-09\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title: Slate and Operations Specialist  Reports To: Associate Director of Admission Status: Full-Time, Exempt  Modality: Onsite Summary/objective Reporting to the Associate Director of Admissions, the Slate and Operations Specialist supports the Admissions office with the execution, auditing, planning, process review, and the evaluation of all aspects related to initiating and completing applications for the Admissions Office. This position will also assist with the maintenance, monitoring, and improvement of the CRM (Slate) functions. Essential functions Serve as an administrator for the Slate CRM, managing system configuration, maintenance, optimization, and ongoing enhancements in support of undergraduate admissions operations.  Design, build, and maintain Slate functionality including applications, forms, portals, reader workflows, communication plans, configurable joins, datasets, queries, reports, rules, permissions, and automations.  Lead the continuous assessment and optimization of Slate functionality by researching new features, best practices, and system enhancements to maximize platform capabilities.  Develop and maintain data integrations between Slate, the Student Information System (Jenzabar), Axiom, testing vendors, financial aid systems, and other third-party applications while ensuring data integrity and accuracy. Monitor, troubleshoot, and resolve complex system, integration, and data issues across Slate and related enterprise systems. Establish and maintain data governance standards through regular auditing, validation, duplicate management, and reconciliation of admissions and enrollment data.  Manage the import and validation of prospect, applicant, and testing data including purchased search names, SAT/ACT, AP, Common App, and other external data sources.  Build and maintain advanced reporting and dashboards that support operational decision-making, enrollment management, and institutional reporting. Collaborate with Information Technology, Financial Aid, Registrar, and Enrollment leadership on system enhancements, integrations, and strategic initiatives. Oversee applicant-facing Slate functionality, including the applicant portal, ensuring an intuitive and effective user experience while resolving escalated technical issues.  Manage and optimize document management processes, application review workflows, and electronic records to ensure efficient processing and compliance.  Configure and maintain financial aid data imports and related applicant communications within Slate. Develop documentation, standard operating procedures, and training materials for Slate users across the admissions team.  Provide functional training, and ongoing support for admissions staff, promoting effective use of Slate and adoption of best practices. Recommend and implement process improvements through automation, workflow redesign, and emerging technologies. Participate in recruitment and yield activities (e.g. open houses, information sessions, admitted student programs) as needed. Skills/Abilities Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with high attention to detail. Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to train team members on CRM functions and proper use. Ability to collaborate effectively across departments and functional areas. Proficiency with Microsoft Excel and Word. Accurate and efficient data input skills with an eye for detail. Comfortable learning and adapting to new   technologies and software. Experience working in a highly collaborative diverse environment with the ability to maintain confidentiality of data. Participate in on campus recruitment and yield events, including but not limited to Open Houses, Information Sessions, and Accepted Student Days. Maintain a broad knowledge base about the College, its programs and opportunities. Maintain broad knowledge base about general trends in secondary and higher education. Supervisory responsibilities  This position has no supervisory responsibilities or direct reports. Work environment Office Setting: Cubicles, open desks, or private offices with access to necessary tools like computers, phones, and office supplies. Remote Setting: Working from home or another location with access to virtual communication platforms and necessary technology. Physical demands Sitting: Ability to remain in a stationary position and operate a computer for extended periods. Typing/Computer Use: Frequent use of a computer keyboard and mouse. Vision Requirements: Ability to read and view screens for extended periods. Speaking/Hearing: Regular communication with coworkers and clients in person, over the phone, or via video calls. Lifting/Carrying: Occasionally lifting or moving items/boxes up to 40 pounds. Reaching/Bending: Periodic reaching for or bending to access files, supplies, or equipment. Mobility: Walking short distances within the office or to meeting rooms. Schedule requirement Occasional evening and weekend work to support recruitment events. Required education and experience Bachelor’s degree. Minimum of 1 year of experience in Higher education, admissions, or Slate/data operations. Demonstrated experience managing data, processes, and systems in a complex, collaborative environment.   Preferred education and experience Experience working in Slate or another admissions/enrollment technology platform. Work authorization/security clearance requirements Must be authorized to work in the United States. MSMC does not sponsor employment visas at this time. EEO statement Mount Saint Mary College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Other duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits Medical Dental Vision 403(b) Retirement Plan (Pre-Tax & Roth Options) 403(b) Employer Match  4 Weeks Paid Vacation per fiscal year (pro-rated at time of hire) 3 Personal Days per fiscal year (pro-rated at time of hire) 1 Floating Holiday per fiscal year 21 Paid College Observed Holidays per fiscal year Employee Assistance Program Voluntary Life Voluntary AD&D Voluntary Hospital Insurance Voluntary Critical Illness Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts – Health, Dependent Care College Paid Life Insurance College Paid Long Term Disability Tuition Remission – Self and Dependents  Tuition Exchange Program",
