    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201235667289_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Instructional Support Specialist",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-26\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title: Instructional Support Specialist  Reports To: Director of Digital Learning & Instructional Design Services Status: Full-Time, Non-Exempt, 35 Hours per Week Modality: On Campus  Summary/objective The Instructional Support Specialist supports Mount Saint Mary College’s digital learning operations by providing faculty and student support for the learning management system (LMS) and related instructional technologies. Responsibilities include delivering training and troubleshooting assistance, developing support resources, assisting with online learning orientation programs, supporting faculty communications and technology initiatives, and contributing to the day-to-day operations of the office. Essential functions Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions. Serve as a primary point of support for faculty in the effective use of the LMS for face-to-face, hybrid, and fully online instruction through training, consultative, and troubleshooting services. Support the office in the design and delivery of trainings and workshops focused on effective use of the LMS in instruction.  Develop resources (e.g., documentation, video tutorials, support materials) for LMS use and technology-enhanced instruction. Assist faculty with the development and editing of instructional content for online placement, including audio, video, and other multimedia.  Support the design and delivery of the Online Learning Student Orientation Tutorial (OLSOT) for students enrolled in hybrid and online courses, including management of the OLSOT hold. Provide support in the development of “Digital Teaching Toolkits” and other faculty messaging via email and newsletters throughout the year. Provide secondary support to instructional design projects such as course development, as assigned by the Director. Provide office support with daily administrative tasks, such as maintaining office calendars, assisting in the production of the Annual Report and other types of research reports, and ordering supplies on behalf of the office.  Assist in maintaining the office’s web presence, including the office’s resource website and social media.  Represent the office by participating in committees, as requested by the Director. Assume other relevant duties, as assigned by the Director. Supervisory responsibilities  This position has no supervisory responsibilities or direct reports. Work environment Office Setting: Cubicles, open desks, or private offices with access to necessary tools like computers, phones, and office supplies. Remote Setting: Working from home or another location with access to virtual communication platforms and necessary technology. Physical demands Sitting: Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk or workstation. Typing/Computer Use: Frequent use of a computer keyboard and mouse. Vision Requirements: Ability to read and view screens for extended periods. Speaking/Hearing: Regular communication with faculty, staff, students, and colleagues in person, over the phone, or via video calls. Lifting/Carrying: Occasionally lifting or moving items up to 10–15 pounds, such as office supplies, laptops, or documents. Reaching/Bending: Periodic reaching for or bending to access files, supplies, or equipment. Mobility: Walking short distances within the office or to meeting rooms. Travel required None Required education and experience Bachelor's degree in Education, Communications, Educational Technology, Business Administration, or a related field. Exceptional written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong customer service orientation with the ability to provide timely and professional support to faculty, staff, and students. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, including Outlook, Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and Teams. Ability to learn and support new software applications and educational technologies. Ability to manage multiple priorities, maintain accurate records, and perform administrative tasks with strong attention to detail. Preferred education and experience 1–2 years of experience in higher education, faculty support, academic technology support, customer service, training, or a related field. Experience using or supporting a learning management system (e.g., Moodle, Canvas, Blackboard, Brightspace). Experience developing training materials, user guides, tutorials, or other support documentation. Experience creating or editing basic multimedia content, including videos, presentations, or web-based resources. Familiarity with online, hybrid, and technology-enhanced learning environments. Work authorization/security clearance requirements Must be authorized to work in the United States. MSMC does not sponsor employment visas at this time. EEO statement Mount Saint Mary College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. Other duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties, or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. Benefits Medical Dental Vision 403(b) Retirement Plan (Pre-Tax & Roth Options) 403(b) Employer Match  Generous Paid Time Off Paid Holidays EAP Voluntary Life Voluntary AD&D Voluntary Hospital Insurance Voluntary Critical Illness Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts – Health, Dependent Care College Paid Life Insurance College Paid Long Term Disability Tuition Remission – Self and Dependents  Tuition Exchange Program",
      "department": ""
    },
    "https://workforcenow.adp.com/mascsr/default/mdf/recruitment/recruitment.html?cid=9553338f-c93c-40ce-9a23-04b38f1294de&ccId=19000101_000001&jobId=9201236721843_1&lang=en_US": {
      "title": "Security Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-21\n\nLocation: Newburgh\n\nJob Title: Security Officer Reports To: Director of Security and Safety Status:  Full-Time, Non-Exempt, 40 hours per week Shift: 4:00pm to 12:00am Summary/objective The Security Officer is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure campus environment through proactive patrol, response to incidents, and engagement with the campus community. This role supports the safety of students, faculty, staff, and visitors by enforcing college policies, responding to emergencies, and providing excellent customer service. Essential functions Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform these essential functions. Provide general campus security through vehicle patrol, foot patrol, and fixed post assignments.  Respond to alarms, calls for service, and emergency situations in a timely manner.  Detect, deter, and investigate unusual or suspicious activity.  Provide information, assistance, and support to students, employees, and visitors.  Observe and report violations of campus policies and applicable laws.  Enforce college regulations, including motor vehicle and parking policies.  Complete clear, accurate, and timely security incident reports.  Deliver excellent customer service in all interactions.  Provide first aid as needed, including use of AED and administering CPR.  Respond to assignments as directed by dispatch or supervisory personnel.  Identify, document, and report unsafe conditions; take corrective action when possible. Perform dispatching duties as assigned, including:  Answering incoming calls Monitoring cameras, access control, and fire systems Monitoring radio communications Maintaining accountability for department property  Perform additional safety and security functions as directed.  Supervisory responsibilities  The position of security officer does not have any direct reports. Work environment Outdoor and indoor campus environment, including patrol of buildings, parking lots, and roadways.  Exposure to varying weather conditions during patrol duties.  Work may include evenings, nights, weekends, and holidays.  Occasional high-stress situations requiring quick decision-making. Physical demands Extensive walking and standing for prolonged periods during foot patrols across campus, including buildings, stairwells, parking lots, and roadways.  Ability to climb stairs, navigate uneven terrain, and move quickly between locations.  Ability to respond rapidly to emergency situations, which may include running, bending, kneeling, or crouching.  Ability to move 75 pounds and lift 40 pounds when necessary.  Frequent use of hands for operating radios, computers, and other security equipment.  Visual and auditory acuity sufficient to observe surroundings, monitor security systems, and respond to alarms and incidents.  Ability to work in varying environmental conditions, including outdoor weather extremes such as heat, cold, rain, or snow. Travel required  The security officer position doesn’t require travel other than local movement throughout campus. Required education and experience High school diploma or GED Minimum of two (2) years of experience as a security officer, police officer, firefighter, or related field  Ability to read, write, and communicate effectively in order to complete reports, understand instructions, and respond to emergency situations Valid New York State driver’s license  Current New York State security guard certification  Ability to work independently with minimal supervision  Basic computer skills, including email, report writing systems, and online training platforms  Ability to effectively respond to emergency situations with urgency and sound judgment Preferred education and experience Some college coursework or military experience  Prior experience in a higher education or campus setting  CPR/AED certification  Benefits Medical Dental Vision 403(b) Retirement Plan (Pre-Tax & Roth Options) 403(b) Employer Match  Generous Paid Time Off Paid Holidays EAP Voluntary Life Voluntary AD&D Voluntary Hospital Insurance Voluntary Critical Illness Insurance Flexible Spending Accounts – Health, Dependent Care College Paid Life Insurance College Paid Long Term Disability Tuition Remission – Self and Dependents  Tuition Exchange Program Work authorization/security clearance requirements Must be authorized to work in the United States. MSMC does not sponsor employment visas at this time. EEO statement Mount Saint Mary College is an Equal Opportunity Employer committed to creating an inclusive and diverse workplace. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. We actively encourage applications from individuals of all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives.   Other duties Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee for this job. Duties, responsibilities and activities may change at any time with or without notice.",
      "department": ""
    }
  },
